.	http://purl.oclc.org/NET/cmcs/schema/:hasConfigurations		<rdf:Bag xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" > <rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/chemsys.mvm" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/BasisSet.ecce_basisset" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/SetupParams" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li></rdf:Bag>
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, B3LYP/6-31G*, relaxed scan of the C-C-C-C torsion, -180 to 180 degrees in 25 points. This calculation shows the conformers of butane: in the Relaxed Scan panel the anti conformer at +-180 degrees is the minimum, 0.0 kJ/mol; the gauche conformers at +-60 degrees lie 3.7 and 3.8 kJ/mol above it, and the syn (eclipsed) geometry at 0 degrees is 23.8 kJ/mol above it, the top of the barrier between the two gauche conformers (electronic energies, no zero-point correction).
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ECCE-QM
